Nope. The implication of the geometric distribution is that you'll
stop after success. What you really are interested in is the expected
value:

http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expected_value

which is the expected number of successes over a string of trails.
The expected value at a 10% success rate over 10 trails is 1. Now
you may get that success on the 1st try, the 7th, or the 10th. You
may get 2 or 3 successes. You may even get 10 strait successes in a
row. But the expected value is the expected number of successes over
the span. On 10 donation you expect to get 1 point of protection.

